{
 "version": 1,
 "about": "NLM-1 D1 curated TRADER VOCABULARY for registry-derived routing (routingV2). Each term: a lower-case phrase matched on word boundaries (a trailing * matches any word ending; an inner * matches one word) -> the routing groups it points at (weight 0..1; 1 = the phrase on its own names that group). DATA, reviewed by hand: a term only ADDS candidate groups the model may SEE; every op is still re-validated against the full registry, the approval policy and the protected-layout checks. Every group named must exist in routing.js GROUPS (nlm1Vocabulary.test.js). `related`: the groups a follow-up to the last capability's group plausibly needs next (conversation context). `entities`: what an entity shape (capabilityIndex.entityTokens) adds to a group's vocabulary weight.",
 "reviewed": {
  "by": "nlm1 track B",
  "date": "2026-11-04",
